## Build result: blocked by environment, not by our changes

Compilation confirmed exactly what I suspected earlier:

```
Cannot find a Java installation on your machine matching this tasks requirements: 
{languageVersion=21, vendor=any, implementation=vendor-specific} for WINDOWS on x86_64.
No locally installed toolchains match and toolchain download repositories have not been configured.
```

`build.gradle` requires Java 21 via toolchain (`JavaLanguageVersion.of(21)`), but this machine only has JDK 8 and JDK 17 installed, and Gradle can't auto-download a JDK 21 while offline. I also had to pass placeholder `-PREPO_USER`/`-PREPO_PWD` values just to get the script to evaluate (the real ones are presumably in `b.bat`/CI, not local `gradle.properties`).

**This isn't a failure caused by our changes** — it's a pre-existing environment gap (no JDK 21 + no network here). I couldn't get further than dependency/toolchain resolution on this machine. Real compilation needs to happen on the other machine, which presumably has JDK 21 and network access to your internal artifact repo.

