## Applying it on the other machine

Copy the `.bundle` file over (USB, network share, etc.), then in your existing clone of the `IVSPersistence` repo on that machine:

```bash
git bundle verify /path/to/wildfly-emer-cleanup.bundle
```

```bash
git fetch /path/to/wildfly-emer-cleanup.bundle wildfly-emer-cleanup:wildfly-emer-cleanup backup/wildfly-before-emer-cleanup:backup/wildfly-before-emer-cleanup
```

```bash
git checkout wildfly-emer-cleanup
```

Then build it there where JDK 21 and network access actually exist:

```bash
./gradlew build test
```

(or `gradle build test` if you use a system install, same as I did here). If it needs real `REPO_USER`/`REPO_PWD`, those are already in your normal dev setup on that machine (or in `b.bat`, though I'd recommend rotating that password given it's sitting in plaintext in git history — that's still an open item from earlier).

Once it builds and you've smoke-tested the OTP flow, that branch is ready to push (`git push origin wildfly-emer-cleanup`) and open for team review before it replaces anything on shared `wildfly`.
